positions.description:
Think.Make.Start is a product development course organized by TUM to promote innovation. 

I joined an interdisciplinary team as a product manager to help develop a desirable, viable, and feasible product that will address the problem of personal exposure to air pollutants.  

-Conducted problem interviews;
-Developed a sustainable business model;
-Developed market entry strategy.

As part of the CDTM program and their Trend Seminar course, I explored the technical, social, economic, and regulatory landscape influencing the today and tomorrow of German SMEs. Together with a team of 25 talented students having diverse cultural and educational backgrounds, I had a chance to help the project partner Bayern Innovativ, which combines extensive expertise in supporting innovations at German SMEs, in identifying new business models and key technologies shaping the future of the Mittelstand companies. 

- Co-author of a comprehensive 200-page Trend Report, covering technical, social, economic, and regulatory dimensions;
- Co-developed a start-up idea for a water waste management solution relevant for SMEs focusing on production;    
- Learned and applied creativity tactics such as TRIZ.

FINN is one of the German fastest-growing start-ups that is revolutionizing traditional car ownership. The company needed efficient in-house products to help them keep up with the hyper-growth. I focused on developing a scalable billing tool for Sales and RevOps teams. 

- Led product development from discovery to delivery: conducting problem interviews, mapping user stories, writing feature specs and DODs for developers, making sure that each feature delivers in accordance to the preset business goals; 
- Rallied multiple stakeholders around the product vision, ensuring their requirements were incorporated into product decisions;
- Iteratively delivered product functionality that met predefined product goals on time.

ILF offers consulting services in the fields of oil and gas, renewable energy systems and electrical grid studies. Following my passion for cleantech and striving to apply my knowledge in electricity transmission systems, I provided engineering consultancy in the integration of photovoltaic systems in distribution grids in Africa. 

-Designed electricity grid, dimensioning of grid components;
-Calculated and analyzed load flows using PSS SINCAL;  
-Modelled network expansion scenarios and faults.

In addition to my deep engineering dive at ILF, I also supported business units in:

-Created customer materials, capability statements, and project reports;
-Investigated new business opportunities such as tenders and project partners.

Motius is an R&D company specializing in emerging technologies. Having joined as a project owner, I had a chance to put gained knowledge in agile project management into practice. Leading 3 projects in the fields of computer vision, power electronics, and LiDAR, I:

-Was responsible for project controlling;
-Organized and moderated workshops with customers and teams' meetings;
-Presented project results to the customers; 
-Met customer’s expectations and extended a project contract.

During my research work at the Center, I helped a professor conduct research for his doctoral dissertation. 

-Researched combined circuits 10 kV (Overhead Power Transmission Lines + Cable Lines) and their exploitation problems;
-Collected the findings in a scientific paper “Exploitation problems of electricity transmission networks with overhead and cable power transmission lines”.
